virglrenderer: float math written to integer outputs keeps its bits

What: SQRT, LRP, DP2/DP3/DP4/DPH, DST, LIT, EXP, LOG, SCS, RCP, RSQ, MAD, POW
and XPD wrote their result with only the destination's type constructor, so a
float result going to an integer output became uint(x) (value converted) or
did not compile (vec4 assigned to a uvec4). They now add the destination's
bit cast like the other ops (floatBitsToUint/floatBitsToInt); for float
destinations nothing changes (the cast is empty).
Why: the guest's TGSI folds floatBitsToUint(f(x)) into "f OUT[n], x" when OUT[n]
is an integer render target. dEQP-GLES3 builtin_functions.precision.sqrt/length
read 315 for sqrt(99463) instead of its bits; SQRT/LRP into such an output were
refused by the host compiler and stopped the guest context. Same on Linux hosts.
Upstream bug (same code upstream); upstreamable; not sent.
Applies after virgl-shader-core-glsl-version.patch.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-core-glsl-shaders.c "... into an integer color output"
(fail without this patch).
